  layout: "[left legend (W cols)] [sep col(s), all-6] [canvas] [optional: sep col(s) | right legend]"
  legend_panels: 1-2 panels; legend_w = unit_size + 2 (4-7 cols); each panel is full-height
  legend_vertical_structure:
    unit_sprite: NxN (N=2-5), fully filled (no 0s), exactly 2 non-{0,6} colors; starts at row 1, 0-padded border; solver color-swaps (a<->b) on read
    gap: 1-6 all-0 rows
    frame: HxW mask (H=4-8, W=3-5) drawn with single non-{0,6} color on 0-bg; must be 8-connected (not necessarily 4-connected); active cells 9-17; fill rate 50-65% (active/total); frame_color disjoint from unit colors
    gap: 0-6 all-0 rows
    marker_square: always at rows h-8 to h-4; 5x5 with color-6 border, 3x3 inner has exactly 1 color-4 pixel at (r,c) in 0..2 encoding anchor (start/middle/end)
    rotation_patch: rows h-3 to h-1; 3x3 with color-7 clock-hand (2 pixels from center toward up/right/down/left = 0/90/180/270 deg)
  canvas:
    width: grid_w minus legend+separator cols; height: grid_h
    background: 2-4 non-{0,6} colors in bands/grid/nested-rings pattern [observed: usually 2 colors in uniform horizontal or vertical stripes]
    constraint: canvas bg colors must be disjoint from unit sprite colors (both panels)
  composite:
    build: tile color-swapped unit into each active frame cell -> (fh*uh) x (fw*uw)
    rotate: rot90 by -k (k from rotation patch)
    place: anchor_to_topleft maps (pr,pc) to canvas offset; composite must fit fully (no clipping)
    overlay: non-{0,6} composite pixels overwrite canvas; canvas color-6 pixels preserved; when multiple composites exist, they must not overlap (no shared non-{0,6} pixels)

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Choose grid_h in 20-30, grid_w=30, num_legends in {1,2}.
    2. Per legend, pick unit_size N in 2-5; legend_w = N+2. Compute canvas_w = grid_w - legend widths - separator widths.
    3. Per legend, design unit_sprite (NxN, 2 colors, fully filled), frame mask (H x W, single color, 8-connected, active cells = 50-65% of H*W), anchor (pr,pc) in {0,1,2}^2, rotation k in {0,1,2,3}.
    4. Compute rotated composite size; ensure it fits within canvas_h x canvas_w at chosen anchor. For 2 legends, ensure composites don't overlap. Reject/resample if not.
    5. Build canvas background with 2 colors in horizontal or vertical bands (band width >= 4).
    6. Build output by overlaying each rotated composite at its anchor position.
    7. Build input by placing unmodified canvas (no overlay) into the grid, adding legend columns with unit sprite (color-swapped back), frame, marker square, and rotation patch, separated by all-6 columns.
    8. Validate via solver.

